1
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:32,280
Look.

2
00:01:34,039 --> 00:01:34,600
Over there.

3
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:35,160
Okay.

4
00:01:43,759 --> 00:01:44,360
Shiya.

5
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:46,280
To be honest,

6
00:01:47,039 --> 00:01:50,080
do you think the big data social intelligent algorithm I made

7
00:01:50,080 --> 00:01:51,880
really has any meaning to exist?

8
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:55,250
Why are you asking this all of a sudden?

9
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:00,650
I always thought in the past

10
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:03,050
that life could not be changed,

11
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:05,620
and a person's life

12
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:07,960
was like a string of precise data.

13
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:09,729
All I needed to do

14
00:02:09,919 --> 00:02:11,760
was extract this data

15
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:13,840
and hand it over to the intelligent algorithm

16
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:14,760
to help people

17
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:18,340
increase the probability of meeting their destined ones.

18
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:19,760
But now I regret it.

19
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,160
I actually feel

20
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:23,690
that I'd rather believe

21
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:26,079
the clock of fate has never stopped.

22
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:35,560
However,

23
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:37,720
your algorithm has a bug.

24
00:02:37,720 --> 00:02:39,380
I've been wanting to tell you.

25
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:42,000
What are you 'ah'-ing about?

26
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,120
Don't question my professionalism

27
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:44,600
as a data maintenance engineer.

28
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:45,320
Your system...

29
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:46,160
How is that possible?

30
00:02:46,160 --> 00:02:48,760
There's no way the system I built has a problem.

31
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:50,240
Why couldn't the system you built have a problem?

32
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:51,079
Listen to me.

33
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:53,730
The system I built has been tested many times.

34
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:54,560
It doesn't...

35
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:56,320
It's burnt.

36
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:57,250
Look at this.

37
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:00,260
No, don't change the subject.

38
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:02,770
How could the system I built have a bug?

39
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:23,040
I always feel

40
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:24,930
that everyone in this universe

41
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:26,160
is a line of code,

42
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:28,360
and even time itself is.

43
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:30,220
Do you think so?

44
00:03:56,960 --> 00:03:58,020
Don't get me wrong.

45
00:03:58,160 --> 00:03:59,000
I just thought

46
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:01,560
it might be more comfortable leaning on me.

47
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:31,800
Shiya.

48
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:33,440
Pei Song.

49
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:35,200
Shiya.

50
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:37,080
Shiya.

51
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:37,960
Where are you?

52
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:39,520
Pei Song.

53
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:40,840
Over there.

54
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:41,760
Shiya.

55
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:43,440
Shiya.

56
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:44,840
Shiya.

57
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:45,360
Brother.

58
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:45,840
Shiya.

59
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:50,400
Shiya.

60
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:53,040
Shiya.

61
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:55,240
I finally found you.

62
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:03,120
Thank you for your hard work.

63
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:03,720
It's nothing.

64
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:04,560
Let's go back first.

65
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:05,890
As long as we found them.

66
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:09,480
Slow down.

67
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:10,880
We're going back.

68
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:16,920
Check the dashcam of that SUV.

69
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:19,280
I suspect someone tampered with it.

70
00:05:19,880 --> 00:05:20,480
Okay.

71
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:24,240
This time,

72
00:05:24,680 --> 00:05:27,140
I will definitely investigate thoroughly.

73
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:30,680
I won't let Shiya die again.

74
00:05:33,159 --> 00:05:34,400
The dashcam is gone.

75
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:35,610
Yes, Mr. Pei.

76
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:37,640
I got to the parking lot as soon as possible,

77
00:05:37,640 --> 00:05:39,320
and the dashcam was already gone.

78
00:05:39,320 --> 00:05:39,960
Mr. Pei.

79
00:05:39,960 --> 00:05:42,240
Could it have been thrown out during the crash

80
00:05:42,240 --> 00:05:43,600
and fell into the mountains?

81
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:44,360
Impossible.

82
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:46,400
My dashcam was reinforced.

83
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:48,810
Unless someone took it down manually.

84
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:50,580
At first I only suspected,

85
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:52,360
but now I'm almost certain.

86
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:54,620
Someone tampered with my car.

87
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:57,140
Good thing I had a backup plan.

88
00:05:57,880 --> 00:05:59,440
I installed tracking software

89
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:00,600
on the dashcam.

90
00:06:01,880 --> 00:06:02,440
Mr. Pei.

91
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:05,320
You installed tracking software on the dashcam?

92
00:06:05,320 --> 00:06:07,250
Do you want me to notify the police?

93
00:06:07,920 --> 00:06:08,560
Mr. Pei.

94
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:10,840
Mr. Pei.

95
00:06:12,560 --> 00:06:13,960
I'll handle this myself.

96
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,260
You can go back to work.

97
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:52,460
Did you need me for something?

98
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:53,520
Why?

99
00:06:53,520 --> 00:06:54,480
Why what?

100
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:56,600
Why did you take the dashcam?

101
00:06:57,720 --> 00:06:59,180
I don't know what you mean.

102
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:00,760
I'll go cook for you.

103
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:02,020
What do you want to eat?

104
00:07:13,880 --> 00:07:15,440
Give me the dashcam.

105
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:17,720
Are you hiding something from me?

106
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:19,640
Or do you know who the killer is?

107
00:07:19,640 --> 00:07:21,370
What does he have to do with you?

108
00:07:23,520 --> 00:07:25,980
There are some things you don't need to know.

109
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:27,650
Why don't I need to know?

110
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:29,680
On this trip,

111
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:31,240
first there was a problem with the rope,

112
00:07:31,240 --> 00:07:32,480
and then the car.

113
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:34,040
I don't want to just watch you

114
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:35,240
die in front of me.

115
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:41,240
You are my wife.

116
00:07:41,440 --> 00:07:42,480
I am your husband.

117
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,400
It is my duty and obligation to protect you.

118
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:47,680
Not for long.

119
00:07:52,080 --> 00:07:53,140
What are you doing?

120
00:08:00,840 --> 00:08:01,640
Let me go.

121
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:28,720
Last time,

122
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:32,020
the person who killed you also came on a motorcycle.

123
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:43,919
Last time?

124
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:47,240
You were reborn.

125
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:51,720
How do you know?

126
00:09:05,080 --> 00:09:06,120
What exactly happened last time?

127
00:09:06,120 --> 00:09:07,180
Don't talk for now.

128
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:14,850
Every time you die in front of me...

129
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:16,040
I am always reborn.

130
00:09:17,560 --> 00:09:20,290
I don't know how many more times this will happen.

131
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:22,480
But this time,

132
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:25,760
I won't let anyone hurt you again.

133
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:27,840
Actually,

134
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:29,760
I know you're reborn.

135
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:34,890
What did you say?

136
00:09:36,160 --> 00:09:38,290
You said it before when you were drunk.

137
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:41,330
Right after we got married.

138
00:09:42,240 --> 00:09:43,770
Right after we got married?

139
00:09:49,080 --> 00:09:50,480
Are you willing to believe me?
